# Auto-detect text files and normalize them to LF line endings in the repository; Git
# still converts to whatever line ending fits the platform on checkout unless a rule
# below overrides that for a specific file.
* text=auto

# The Gradle wrapper's Unix shell script needs LF endings to run at all -- if this ever
# gets committed with CRLF endings (easy to do by accident from Windows), `./gradlew`
# breaks for every Linux/Mac contributor. Pin both wrapper scripts explicitly so this
# can't happen regardless of the committer's platform or Git config.
gradlew text eol=lf
gradlew.bat text eol=crlf

# Common binary types -- don't let Git try to diff or line-ending-normalize these.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.ico binary
*.jks binary
*.keystore binary
